 "title": "y = 3x² becomes a straight line on log axes",
 "caption": "Taking logs of y = 3x² gives log y = log 3 + 2 log x. Plotting log y against log x gives a straight line of slope 2 (the exponent) and intercept log 3 ≈ 0.477 (the constant).",
 "alt": "A straight line rising with slope 2 from intercept 0.477 on the vertical axis, plotted against log x.",
 "description": [
  "Take logs of both sides: log y = log 3 + 2 log x.",
  "Plot log y against log x.",
  "The graph is a straight line.",
  "Its slope 2 is the exponent and its intercept log 3 gives the constant 3."
 ],
